# Ubuntu Vanilla ISO Builder - Example Configuration File
# ========================================================
#
# NOTE: Config files are an ADVANCED MODE feature. You must use --advanced
# (or pick Advanced at the startup mode prompt) for config files to be loaded.
# In basic mode (default), the build uses interactive prompts and sensible
# defaults instead.
#
# Copy this file to "build.cfg" (in the scripts/ directory) for automatic loading
# in advanced mode, or use --advanced --config=/path/to/your-config.cfg -
#
# You can also generate this file interactively with:
#   ./build.sh --generate-config
#
# CLI arguments always override values from this file.
# Lines starting with # are comments. Inline comments are supported when the
# "#" is preceded by whitespace (values themselves may contain "#").
#
# Usage:
#   cp build.cfg.example build.cfg
#   # Edit values below, then:
#   ./build.sh --advanced -
#   # Or explicitly:
#   ./build.sh --advanced --config=build.cfg -
#
# Note on the trailing '-': it means "run every build stage" and is OPTIONAL.
#   ./build.sh --advanced --config=build.cfg       # equivalent: runs all stages
#   ./build.sh --advanced --config=build.cfg -     # equivalent: also runs all stages
# You only need it when restricting to a stage range, e.g. `setup_host - build_iso`.

# --- Core Build Settings ---
# TARGET_UBUNTU_VERSION=noble          # jammy | noble | resolute
# TARGET_UBUNTU_MIRROR=https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/
# TARGET_KERNEL_FLAVOR=generic         # generic | lowlatency
# TARGET_INSTALLER=calamares           # calamares | ubiquity (ubiquity: jammy only) | cli-installer (server ISO only)
# TARGET_DESKTOP=gnome                 # gnome | xfce | lxde | lxqt | mate | cinnamon | budgie | kde-plasma
#                                      # also: none | server | cli | headless | minimal (TTY-only ISO; pairs with TARGET_INSTALLER=cli-installer)

# --- Desktop-Specific ---
# TARGET_KDE_PACKAGE=kde-standard      # kde-full | kde-standard | kde-plasma-desktop
# TARGET_MATE_PACKAGE=mate-desktop-environment  # mate-desktop-environment | mate-desktop-environment-core
# TARGET_MATE_EXTRAS=0                 # 0 | 1
# TARGET_GNOME_INSTALL_RECOMMENDS=0    # 0 | 1

# --- Browser Options ---
# TARGET_BRAVE_CHANNEL=release         # none | release | origin
# TARGET_LIBREWOLF=0                   # 0 | 1
# TARGET_FIREFOX=0                     # 0 | 1
# TARGET_FIREFOX_ESR=0                 # 0 | 1
# TARGET_FIREFOX_POPOS=0               # 0 | 1 (build-popos.sh only: native Firefox deb from the Pop!_OS repo, not a snap stub)
# TARGET_THUNDERBIRD=0                 # 0 | 1

# --- Package Managers ---
# TARGET_PACSTALL=1                    # 0 | 1 (install Pacstall; default: yes)

# --- Optional Extras ---
# TARGET_UBUNTU_STUDIO=0              # 0 | 1
# TARGET_SYSTEM76_DRIVER=0            # 0 | 1 (build-popos.sh only: system76-driver for System76 hardware)

# --- Optional Services & Tools ---
# TARGET_FWUPD=0                      # 0 | 1 (pre-install fwupd; it is blocked during the build either way and can always be apt-installed later)
# TARGET_OPENSSH_SERVER=0             # 0 | 1 (pre-install openssh-server)
# TARGET_COCKPIT=0                    # 0 | 1 (pre-install Cockpit from the ${release}-backports pocket for the latest version)

# --- Locale & Keyboard (for unattended builds) ---
# TARGET_LOCALE=en_US.UTF-8           # e.g. en_US.UTF-8, de_DE.UTF-8, fr_FR.UTF-8
# TARGET_KEYBOARD_LAYOUT=us           # e.g. us, de, fr, gb
# TARGET_KEYBOARD_VARIANT=            # e.g. intl, nodeadkeys (optional)

# --- Output & Workspace ---
# TARGET_NAME=                         # Custom ISO base name (auto-generated if empty)
# GRUB_LIVEBOOT_LABEL=Try Ubuntu without installing
# UBUNTU_VANILLA_WORKSPACE=            # Custom workspace parent directory (default: /var/cache/ubuntu-vanilla-build in basic mode, ~/uvb-workspace in advanced mode)
# UVB_OUTPUT_DIR=                      # Directory for the finished ISO + checksums (default: your home directory)

# --- Advanced Mode ---
# ADVANCED_MODE=0                      # Set to 1 to preserve workspace on failure/interrupt and enable package cache

# --- Hooks ---
# HOOKS_DIR=                           # Custom hooks directory (default: scripts/hooks/)

# --- Interactive Mode ---
# INTERACTIVE=0                        # Set to 0 to disable all interactive prompts
# NO_CONFIRM=1                         # Set to 1 to skip the pre-build confirmation prompt

# --- Server / Minimal ISO preset ---
# Setting TARGET_DESKTOP to one of none|server|cli|headless|minimal switches
# the build to a TTY-only profile: no desktop, no display manager, no Flatpak,
# no browser APT sources. Calamares and Ubiquity are not available on this
# profile; the build forces TARGET_INSTALLER=cli-installer, which ships
# scripts/cli-installer/install-system as the installer. OpenSSH server is
# enabled by default; use TARGET_OPENSSH_SERVER=0 to opt out.
# Browser / desktop-only flags (TARGET_BRAVE_CHANNEL, TARGET_LIBREWOLF,
# TARGET_FIREFOX[_ESR|_POPOS], TARGET_THUNDERBIRD, TARGET_UBUNTU_STUDIO,
# TARGET_KDE_PACKAGE, TARGET_MATE_PACKAGE, TARGET_MATE_EXTRAS,
# TARGET_GNOME_INSTALL_RECOMMENDS) are auto-cleared with a friendly warning
# when this profile is on. See the "Building a Server / Minimal ISO" section
# in the README for the full picture.
#
# Example: a fully unattended Ubuntu 24.04 server ISO with Cockpit on:
#   TARGET_UBUNTU_VERSION=noble
#   TARGET_KERNEL_FLAVOR=generic
#   TARGET_DESKTOP=server
#   TARGET_INSTALLER=cli-installer
#   TARGET_OPENSSH_SERVER=1
#   TARGET_COCKPIT=1
#
# For a Pop!_OS server ISO, mirror the same lines into scripts/build-popos.cfg
# (its own config file in the same directory).

# --- Server / Minimal ISO ("No Desktop") ---
# Set TARGET_DESKTOP to one of: none, server, cli, headless, minimal
# to build a TTY-only ISO. The CLI installer
# (scripts/cli-installer/install-system) is auto-selected; openssh-server
# is pre-installed by default; browser, Flatpak, GNOME-app purges, and
# Plymouth are all skipped.
#
# Example unattended server ISO build:
#   TARGET_DESKTOP=server
#   TARGET_INSTALLER=cli-installer
#   TARGET_OPENSSH_SERVER=1
#   TARGET_COCKPIT=1                  # optional: web admin console from ${release}-backports
#
# Equivalent CLI invocation:
#   ./build.sh --release=noble --kernel=generic --desktop=server -
